From 077216d576bae8b1afcee58ab75a95da6783f8e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:22:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 22/34] vulkan: conv_step also does the q/k L2_NORM of the
 gated-delta-net layers

One 128-channel head per workgroup; for the q and k heads it reduces |y|^2 and writes y / max(|y|, eps) into the
L2_NORM output, which is skipped: -48 barriers and launches per Bonsai decode token. GGML_VK_DISABLE_CONV_L2
keeps the separate L2_NORM. Test: CONV_STEP now checks the L2 output too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp          | 45 ++++++++++++--
 .../ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/conv_step.comp | 59 ++++++++++++++-----
 tests/test-backend-ops.cpp                    | 12 +++-
 3 files changed, 92 insertions(+), 24 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp
